{Sicilian Defense: Mengarini Variation. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. a3 c5 2. e4 g6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. Nxd4 Bg7 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Be3 Nf6 7. Nc3 O-O 8. Nb3 ! d6 {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... Nb4 Rb1 Na2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Be2 Be6 10. f4 Na5 11. O-O Rc8 ?! 12. f5 Bxb3 13. cxb3 Rxc3 14. bxc3 Nxe4 15. Qc2 Nxc3 16. Rae1 Nxe2+ 17. Qxe2 Nc6 18. Bg5 gxf5 19. Qb5 f6 20. Be3 Qd7 21. Rxf5 e5 22. Qd5+ Rf7 23. Rh5 Ne7 24. Qd3 f5 25. Bc5 Rf6 26. Rd1 Qe8 27. Bxd6 Qxh5 28. Bxe7 Rf7 29. Qd8+ Bf8 30. Bb4 f4 31. Rd7 Qf5 32. Rxf7 Qxf7 33. a4 e4 34. Bxf8 Qxf8 35. Qg5+ Qg7 36. Qd5+ Qf7 37. Qxe4 Qxb3 38. Qe8+ Kg7 39. Qe5+ Kg6 40. Qe4+ Kg5 41. Qe5+ Kg6 42. Qxf4 Qb6+ 43. Kf1 Qf6 44. Qxf6+ Kxf6 45. a5 Ke5 46. Ke1 Kd4 47. Kd2 Kc4 48. Kc2 Kb4 49. a6 bxa6 50. g4 Kc5 51. g5 Kd6 52. h4 Ke7 53. h5 Kf7 54. g6+ hxg6 55. hxg6+ Kxg6 56. Kd3 a5 57. Ke4 a4 58. Kd4 Kf6 59. Kc4 Kg6 60. Kd4 Kh5 61. Kc4 Kh4 {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} 62. Kd4 1/2-1/2
